is this airplane

500
00:17:58,630 --> 00:18:00,610
has six permanent
magnetic generators.

501
00:18:00,610 --> 00:18:03,760
They are the primary source
of flight control power.

502
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,740
All that has to happen is
the engines have to rotate.

503
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:07,348
That's it.

504
00:18:07,348 --> 00:18:08,890
So even if the
engines are shut down,

505
00:18:08,890 --> 00:18:10,810
I can just keep wind
going through the engines

506
00:18:10,810 --> 00:18:12,190
and they rotate,
they will rotate

507
00:18:12,190 --> 00:18:15,040
sufficient to generate power
from the permanent magnetic

508
00:18:15,040 --> 00:18:15,940
generators.

509
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:19,220
If those fail, the airplane
also has electrical generators

510
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:19,720
on board.

511
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,710
There's two of them--
there's actually

512
00:18:20,710 --> 00:18:21,668
three of them on board.

513
00:18:21,668 --> 00:18:24,050
They can power the
flight controls as well.

514
00:18:24,050 --> 00:18:27,520
Worst case scenario for a Raptor
pilot, the engines seize up,

515
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,880
I lose my electrical power.

516
00:18:28,880 --> 00:18:30,678
The only thing I have
left is a battery.

517
00:18:30,678 --> 00:18:32,470
And just like anything
else with a battery,

518
00:18:32,470 --> 00:18:34,220
the more you use it,
the more it depletes.

519
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:36,910
So at that point, any deflection
of the flight control surfaces

520
00:18:36,910 --> 00:18:39,490
depletes the electrical energy
and you don't have that much

521
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:41,470
left to actually control it.

522
00:18:41,470 --> 00:18:42,040
OK.

523
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:44,373
One last thing here and we'll
move on to the next slide.

524
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:47,048
We'll talk a little bit--
just some definitions.

525
00:18:47,048 --> 00:18:48,590
The wing has this
thing on the front.

