1264
00:46:11,010 --> 00:46:12,390
Do you guys know about--

1265
00:46:12,390 --> 00:46:14,223
this gets a little bit
advanced, but a thing

1266
00:46:14,223 --> 00:46:16,947
called static margin,
which is a stability

1267
00:46:16,947 --> 00:46:18,030
thing about this airplane.

1268
00:46:18,030 --> 00:46:21,300
Again, this airplane, in its
bare airframe configuration,

1269
00:46:21,300 --> 00:46:24,630
no hydraulics, no computers,
nothing on board the airplane,

1270
00:46:24,630 --> 00:46:26,400
totally unstable.

1271
00:46:26,400 --> 00:46:28,948
What keeps it stable
is the computer itself.

1272
00:46:28,948 --> 00:46:30,990
What you'll see is you'll
see this maneuver where

1273
00:46:30,990 --> 00:46:32,280
he'll go into a
g turn and you'll

1274
00:46:32,280 --> 00:46:34,860
see all those clouds forming on
the back end of the airplane.

1275
00:46:34,860 --> 00:46:37,440
Pay attention to what the
leading edge flaps are doing.

1276
00:46:37,440 --> 00:46:38,880
They're digging in.

1277
00:46:38,880 --> 00:46:41,010
The horizontal
stabilators, you'll

1278
00:46:41,010 --> 00:46:43,590
see them initially move
to get the turn going,

1279
00:46:43,590 --> 00:46:45,953
but then once
established in the turn,

1280
00:46:45,953 --> 00:46:47,370
the way it's
controlling things is

1281
00:46:47,370 --> 00:46:50,640
it's moving around
the aerodynamic center

1282
00:46:50,640 --> 00:46:52,230
and the center of gravity.

1283
00:46:52,230 --> 00:46:53,762
It's doing that
by dorking around

1284
00:46:53,762 --> 00:46:55,470
a bit with the lift
on the wing, and it's

1285
00:46:55,470 --> 00:46:57,500
doing that by deflecting
the leading edge flaps.

1286
00:46:57,500 --> 00:47:00,000
So that flight control surface
display I showed you earlier,

1287
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:02,520
the horizontal stabilators
would be completely streamlined.

1288
00:47:02,520 --> 00:47:05,790
And all of the maneuvering is
coming from the wing itself,

1289
00:47:05,790 --> 00:47:07,573
which is pretty amazing.

1290
00:47:07,573 --> 00:47:08,490
PROFESSOR: Next video?

1291
00:47:08,490 --> 00:47:08,910
RANDY GORDON: No, no.

1292
00:47:08,910 --> 00:47:09,827
Go to flight controls.

